# Dashboard environment — copy to `.env.local` and fill in.
#
# Nothing here is committed with values; `.env*.local` is gitignored.

# --- Google Maps ----------------------------------------------------------
# Maps JavaScript API. The key is sent from the browser, so it is public by
# nature; the HTTP referrer restriction is what keeps it safe.
#
# Setup:
#   1. Enable the Maps JavaScript API on a Google Cloud project.
#   2. Attach a billing account. Required even to stay inside the free tier.
#   3. Create an API key. Set BOTH restrictions:
#        Application restriction: HTTP referrers → https://localhost:3000/*
#        API restriction:         Maps JavaScript API only
#
# A referrer restriction matches the full URL, so it needs the path wildcard.
# A bare `localhost` does not match.
#
# If you later pass `authReferrerPolicy: 'origin'` to the loader, the referrer
# restriction must then be the domain with NO path. That parameter is opt-in and
# is not currently set.
#
# Free allowance: 10,000 map loads per month, then roughly $7 per 1,000.
#
# Without this value the Map page renders a "Not configured" notice instead of
# attempting to load the SDK.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=
